voxcpm2-ncnn

The project is distributed primarily under the MIT license in LICENSE.

Small portions of the runtime are derivative work of Apache-2.0 licensed
`ncnn_llm` code that was reused and rewritten during the VoxCPM2 port. That
Apache-2.0 scope is limited to these helper families:

- src/tokenizer.cpp: UTF-8 scanning, SentencePiece-style piece splitting,
  byte-token fallback, and VoxCPM2 tokenizer merge application helpers.
- src/synthesizer.cpp: ncnn tensor construction/extraction helpers, VoxCPM2 CFM
  sampling glue, latent layout conversion, and RoPE cache construction.

The Apache-2.0 text is retained in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt for that material.

The local VoxCPM2 SDPA custom layer and embedded Vulkan shaders under
src/ncnn_layers are derived from BSD-3-Clause licensed ncnn SDPA Vulkan layer
and shader code, with local changes for VoxCPM2 graph names, shader embedding,
and runtime integration. The BSD-3-Clause text is retained in
LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt for that material.

Distributed native binaries also contain or accompany ncnn (BSD-3-Clause),
LLVM OpenMP on Linux (Apache-2.0 with LLVM Exceptions), and MoltenVK on Apple
platforms (Apache-2.0). Their applicable texts are retained under `LICENSES`;
see `CREDITS.md` for the platform mapping.
